 ```
 
+Camera mappings may set `image_qos_profile` and `camera_info_qos_profile`
+independently. This is useful when large, perishable raw images should use
+Best Effort delivery while the smaller calibration metadata remains Reliable.
+If either optional key is omitted, that publisher falls back to the shared
+`qos_profile`, preserving existing sensor mappings.
+The optional `best_effort_depth_1` profile is a simulation-only bounded-latest
+variant for large raw images: it uses Best Effort, Volatile, KEEP_LAST history
+with depth 1. The existing `best_effort` profile retains depth 10.
+
 For CARLA sensor parameters, see [CARLA Sensor Reference](https://carla.readthedocs.io/en/latest/ref_sensors/).
 
